Z||000000||Dan87GT||07-09-2001||08:39 AM||||I pulled my tired 2.8 this weekend and I am looking at the ARI 3.4 shortblock anybody have any thoughts about it? I won't be using NOS or a turbo so I am not too concerned about the wall thickness.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-09-2001||11:34 AM||||I've wondered about this also. Not sure what kind of a warranty they offer, but it looks like they offer all kinds of custom goodies, if you buy a long block.<BR>As thin as the cylinder walls are, if it ever needs rebuilding, boring it has got to be out of the question, though.  <BR>There's a guy in our club who has built his own 2.8 into a 3.4 in the same manner. Hasn't had any problems with it, AFAIK. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||6
